Wings patch 0012: an approved plan survives Continue and keeps going

Upstream's agent_loop.build_active_plan_note says the approved plan is
"sent back by the frontend each turn", but static/js/chat.js sent it once
and cleared it. So when a long plan hit the step limit and the person
pressed Continue, the plan was no longer pinned and update_plan was turned
off (a Continue message is not a plan request), and the agent lost track of
which steps were done. OpenManus drives a plan from outside the model, step
after step; this gives Wings the same follow through without giving up its
plan review and approval.

  * static/js/chat.js: the approved plan is remembered per chat for 12
    hours after the last approval or tick, until every step is ticked or the
    person clears it. A Continue, Resume or typed "continue" in that chat
    sends it again, so the plan note is pinned and update_plan is available.
    Only the person's approved text is ever sent: from the agent's
    update_plan only the tick marks of the approved steps are copied, and a
    plan whose steps the agent added, removed or reworded is dropped until
    the person approves it again in the plan panel. When the run that
    carries the plan reaches the step limit with steps left, the chat
    continues on its own, once that reply has fully finished and while the
    person is still in that chat, up to 3 times per approval (the count
    survives a reload), with a Stop here button; approvals, questions and
    the Stop button still pause it as before. It never continues a run the
    loop breaker stopped, and it yields to anything the person sends or is
    typing. Ticks are kept while the chat runs in the background. The
    Execute button under a plan approves the plan shown in that message,
    not the last plan stored for any chat.

